\par\pard\sb240\sa120{\f2\fs28\b\cf1 6. Mathematical Formulas & Core Algorithms}\par\pard\sa80
\par\pard\sb160\sa80{\f2\fs24\b\cf2 A. Haversine Distance & Velocity Equations}\par\pard\sa60
\pard\sb60\sa100\sl276\slmult1{\f0\fs21\cf1 The great-circle distance d between coordinates (lat1, lon1) and (lat2, lon2) is calculated as:}\par
\pard\sb120\sa140\li360\ri360\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf5\pad100{\f1\fs19\cf1 R = 6371.0  # Mean Earth radius in kilometers\line
dlat = radians(lat2 - lat1)\line
dlon = radians(lon2 - lon1)\line
a = sin\u178?(dlat / 2) + cos(radians(lat1)) * cos(radians(lat2)) * sin\u178?(dlon / 2)\line
c = 2 * atan2(sqrt(a), sqrt(1 - a))\line
distance_km = R * c\line
\line
velocity_kmh = distance_km / max(hours_diff, 0.1)\line
# If distance > 350 km and velocity > 800 km/h -> Flag Impossible Travel (+35 pts)}\par
\par\pard\sb160\sa80{\f2\fs24\b\cf2 B. MITRE ATT&CK Sliding-Window Threat Correlation}\par\pard\sa60
\pard\sb60\sa100\sl276\slmult1{\f0\fs21\cf1 Maintains an active sliding window of recent activities (N = 10) to correlate multi-stage kill chains:}\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb40\sa60{\f0\fs21\cf2 \bullet\tab }{\f2\fs21\b\cf1 [MITRE T1110] Brute Force Storm:} {\f0\fs21\cf1 >= 3 failed login attempts within window.}\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb40\sa60{\f0\fs21\cf2 \bullet\tab }{\f2\fs21\b\cf1 [MITRE T1078] Account Takeover Chain:} {\f0\fs21\cf1 Failed logins followed by successful authentication from unrecognized device or location.}\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb40\sa60{\f0\fs21\cf2 \bullet\tab }{\f2\fs21\b\cf1 [MITRE T1048] Data Exfiltration Chain:} {\f0\fs21\cf1 Off-hours or anomalous location login followed by bulk document download.}\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb40\sa60{\f0\fs21\cf2 \bullet\tab }{\f2\fs21\b\cf1 [MITRE T1078.003] Impossible Travel Geo-Anomaly:} {\f0\fs21\cf1 Travel speed between sequential logins exceeds 800 km/h commercial aviation limit.}\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb40\sa60{\f0\fs21\cf2 \bullet\tab }{\f2\fs21\b\cf1 [MITRE T1204] Honeytoken Canary Trap Sprung:} {\f0\fs21\cf1 Unauthorized access attempt on decoy canary file in enterprise vault.}\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb40\sa60{\f0\fs21\cf2 \bullet\tab }{\f2\fs21\b\cf1 [MITRE T1090] Proxy / Tor Anonymization:} {\f0\fs21\cf1 Connection originating from known Tor exit cluster or anonymous proxy.}\par
\par\pard\sb240\sa120{\f2\fs28\b\cf1 7. Viva & Technical Interview Defense Guide}\par\pard\sa80
\par\pard\sb160\sa80{\f2\fs24\b\cf2 Q1: Why use deterministic heuristics rather than a black-box deep learning model?}\par\pard\sa60
\pard\sb60\sa100\sl276\slmult1{\f0\fs21\cf1 A: In mission-critical cybersecurity, explainability is paramount. When an account is quarantined or challenged with MFA, the SOC analyst must be able to audit the exact heuristic violation (e.g. 6,229 km traversed in 1 hour). Heuristics provide immediate, zero-latency, deterministic decisions without training cold-starts.}\par
\par\pard\sb160\sa80{\f2\fs24\b\cf2 Q2: How does the Honeytoken Canary Trap support Zero-Trust?}\par\pard\sa60
\pard\sb60\sa100\sl276\slmult1{\f0\fs21\cf1 A: In Zero-Trust, assume breach. If an attacker bypasses the perimeter or compromises valid credentials, perimeter defenses are blind. A Honeytoken decoy file acts as an active internal tripwire: legitimate personnel have no reason to access it, providing a 100% true-positive indicator of compromise (MITRE T1204).}\par
\par\pard\sb160\sa80{\f2\fs24\b\cf2 Q3: What prevents False Positives in travel detection?}\par\pard\sa60
\pard\sb60\sa100\sl276\slmult1{\f0\fs21\cf1 A: Rather than flagging any location change, CyberShield uses spherical Haversine velocity. If a user travels from Jammu to Delhi in 5 hours (102 km/h), the velocity is physically feasible and is scored as normal. Only velocities exceeding 800 km/h trigger critical alerts.}\par
